WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.483
Step 1. Open the Shared catalogue.

1.2
00:00:02.483 --> 00:00:07.671
A customization takes the slug of a shared valueset and takes its place in your

1.3
00:00:07.671 --> 00:00:15.223
facility. The shared valueset stays unchanged. Select the Shared catalogue tab.

2.1
00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:17.738
Step 2. Start the customization.

2.2
00:00:17.738 --> 00:00:21.418
On the row of the shared valueset, select Customize.

2.3
00:00:21.418 --> 00:00:26.867
Care opens Create ValueSet with the parent and Facility customization already

2.4
00:00:26.867 --> 00:00:28.004
selected.

3.1
00:00:28.004 --> 00:00:32.692
Step 3. Enter the basic information. Give the customization a Name.

3.2
00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:35.606
The Slug is taken from the parent value set.

3.3
00:00:35.606 --> 00:00:40.610
Only an Active customization takes the place of the shared valueset.

4.1
00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.784
Step 4. Change the rules.

4.2
00:00:42.784 --> 00:00:47.477
Use parent rules is on, so your rules add to the shared ones.

4.3
00:00:47.477 --> 00:01:08.293
Add include rules to add codes, and exclude rules to remove codes.

5.1
00:01:08.293 --> 00:01:11.829
Step 5. Preview the codes. This step is optional.

5.2
00:01:11.829 --> 00:01:17.126
With Use parent rules on, the preview shows only the rules that you added here,

5.3
00:01:17.126 --> 00:01:20.107
not the rules of the shared valueset.

6.1
00:01:20.107 --> 00:01:23.487
Step 6. Save the customization. Select Save.

6.2
00:01:23.487 --> 00:01:29.391
Care shows Not Found because the customization stays hidden until it is shared with

6.3
00:01:29.391 --> 00:01:32.879
a department. Your customization is saved.
